   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "so … dass: so … that",
     "texto": [
      "With **so** + adjective or adverb + **dass** one says that something is so strong that it has consequences: **Es regnet so stark, dass wir zu Hause bleiben** (it's raining so hard that we stay at home). The clause with «dass» goes after, with the verb at the end.",
      "With «so» in front and the verb at the end: **so stark, dass**. Watch out: don't confuse it with the «dass» of opinion from lesson 14."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "sodass and daher: so",
     "texto": [
      "**Sodass** means \"so that\" and links a consequence with a full clause: **Der Kurs war voll, sodass alle gehen mussten** (the class was full, so everyone had to leave). **Daher** (that's why) goes like «deshalb»: the verb goes in second position: **Er ist krank, daher bleibt er zu Hause**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
